    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen a copy operation is being done, but a file with the same name as target already exists, the operation fails silently.\r\n\r\nNote that the docs say\r\n```lua\r\n--- - Copying inside same parent directory is supported only if target path has\r\n---   different name.\r\n```\r\nbut, if I understand this correctly, this only disallows something like `cp x x`.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-4e59422\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNo config should be needed except setting up `mini.files` (tested with `NORC`). Do\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ mkdir a b\r\n$ echo a > a/x\r\n$ echo b > b/x\r\n$ nvim b\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn mini.files, yank the `x` file, and then go to the `a` directory and paste the file there. You will see the following prompt (depending on the starting directory):\r\n\r\n```\r\nCONFIRM FILE SYSTEM ACTIONS\r\n\r\n/tmp/b:\r\n    COPY: 'x' to '/tmp/a/x'\r\n\r\n[Y]es, (N)o:\r\n```\r\n\r\nAccept the prompt.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEither the operation should return an error, or `a/x` should contain `b`, like after `cp b/x a/x`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`a/x` contains `a`, as if the operation silently failed.",
